FallenKingsCrown: {
	DisplayName: Fallen King's Crown
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Immunity to fall damage
		Hold DOWN in midair to become a crown dive and plummet
		Falling more than 25 tiles naturally also triggers the dive
		Enemies struck mid-dive are crushed by the crown
		Landing unleashes a gel shockwave; deeper falls hit harder, maxing out at 40 tiles
		The shockwave fires at most once every 1.5 seconds; the crown dims while it recharges
		The impact leaves a gel field that slows enemies inside and drains their health
		Grappling, mounting or entering liquid cancels the dive
		"The day the throne fell, weight itself became the verdict"
		'''
}

BloodfogIris: {
	DisplayName: Bloodfog Iris
	Tooltip:
		'''
		8% increased critical strike chance
		Double tap LEFT, RIGHT or UP to surge that way as blood fog, briefly invulnerable at the start
		Surges have a 1.25 second cooldown; the pupil glow dims while it recharges
		A surge ends in a 1.5 second ambush state: you sink into the fog and draw less attention
		Your next strike during an ambush is a guaranteed critical hit
		Lethal damage dissolves you into blood fog; you reform toward your cursor, briefly invulnerable and already in ambush
		The fog rebirth can occur once every 60 seconds; for 3 seconds after reforming you take 15% more damage
		"The fog has not settled, and the pupil has not closed"
		'''
}

WorldEatersMaw: {
	DisplayName: World-Eater's Maw
	Tooltip:
		'''
		All your attacks add a stack of Corrosion, up to 10 stacks; lasts 6 seconds and refreshes on every hit
		At full stacks, Corrosion strips 15 defense and sears for 20 acid damage per second
		When a corroded enemy dies, a devouring wormling bursts from its corpse to fight for you, at most one every 2 seconds
		Wormlings burrow and ambush nearby foes, biting for 2 stacks and splashing Corrosion around each breach
		Up to 3 wormlings at once, each living for 7 seconds
		"Every edge of the world is a tooth mark it left behind"
		'''
}

MirrorheartParadox: {
	DisplayName: Mirrorheart Paradox
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A mirrored heart drifts at your side
		While the mirrorheart is solid, the moment you take damage you swap places with it, dodging the hit with brief invulnerability
		Heartbeat pulses burst at both swap positions, dealing 90 base damage and confusing enemies for 2.5 seconds
		For 5 seconds after a swap, projectiles you fire are echoed by the mirrorheart at 50% damage
		Summons, held weapons and explosives are not echoed
		Paradox backlash: the next hit you take within 3 seconds of a swap deals 25% more damage
		Swaps occur at most once every 25 seconds; the mirrorheart stays translucent while recharging, with an audible cue when it turns solid again
		"In the mirror, it breaks a heartbeat before you do"
		'''
}

SwarmVortexBeacon: {
	DisplayName: Swarm Vortex Beacon
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hitting enemies stacks Bee Marks; at 8 stacks the target is caught in a swarm vortex
		The vortex grinds its victim for 5 seconds, stinging 4 times per second for 18 base damage each
		Trapped enemies are heavily slowed; bosses are only slightly slowed
		Landing more hits on the victim extends the grip, up to 8 seconds
		Only one vortex is kept at a time; when a new prey's marks fill up, the swarm moves over to it
		When the victim dies, the vortex also transfers to a nearby enemy
		Vortex stings deal 25% more damage while you carry a Hive Pack
		Stand still and the swarm returns to you, crystallizing into a wax ward over your skin
		The wax ward absorbs up to 30 damage and lingers for 5 seconds once you start moving
		A shattered ward takes 3 seconds to crystallize again
		"The Queen's beacon does not summon the swarm - it marks the next prey"
		'''
}

SoulbindingArm: {
	DisplayName: Soulbinding Arm
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Projects a curse domain around you; enemies inside take 8% increased damage from you
		Killing an enemy inside the domain harvests a soul, storing up to 8
		Souls orbit you; each one blocks an enemy projectile in your place, then expires
		Blocked projectiles turn into curseflame orbs hurled back at nearby enemies, dealing 60 base damage
		After each block, the soul ring takes 1 second to reload
		Once the ring is full it gathers briefly, then a spectral hand lunges at the strongest enemy nearby
		The hand deals 300 base damage ignoring defense, scaling with your damage bonuses
		Seized enemies take 20% increased damage from all sources for 5 seconds; regular enemies are also pinned for 1 second
		"The severed arm still harvests souls; its five fingers have never let go"
		'''
}

WhiteoutStormCore: {
	DisplayName: Whiteout Storm Core
	Tooltip:
		'''
		5% damage reduction; immune to Chilled, Frozen, Frostburn and Frostbite
		Taking damage automatically detonates a whiteout storm; lasts 6 seconds, 20 second cooldown
		The storm deals 120 base damage to nearby enemies, confusing them for 3 seconds and whiteblinding them for 6
		Whiteblinded enemies are heavily slowed and take 10 frostbite damage per second
		During the storm you gain an extra 30% damage reduction and knockback immunity, and the snow veil never blocks your sight
		Boss-class enemies cannot be confused and take a greatly reduced slow
		While running on the ground, heaves a row of ice spikes from the earth ahead every second
		Each spike deals 45 base damage and briefly chills enemies
		"Within the whiteout, the blizzard parts only for you"
		'''
}

GluttonousThroat: {
	DisplayName: Gluttonous Throat
	Tooltip:
		'''
		8% of all damage you deal flows back to you as blood beads
		Blood beads skip potion sickness, but restore at most 2% of your max life per second
		Overflow blood splatters onto the ground; Moon Bite seals the throat, and every bead falls astray
		Every 9 seconds a tongue of flesh seizes the farthest enemy within 68 tiles and drags it before you
		Bitten enemies suffer Rotsaw for 5 seconds: 40 life torn per second
		For 2.5 seconds after an enemy is dragged to you, your next strike against it deals double damage
		The executing strike also detonates any remaining Rotsaw as a burst of bonus damage
		Bosses cannot be dragged, but are still bitten, sawed and marked for execution
		"The far end of the throat has no bottom"
		'''
}

RefractionWaltz: {
	DisplayName: Refraction Waltz
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Greatly boosts aerial acceleration and turning
		Cresting a jump, double-jumping, reversing or dashing midair condenses a refraction crystal behind you
		Up to 6 crystals may exist at once; the oldest shatters to make room
		Crystals link up with prism beams in the order they were danced out, closing the loop at six
		Beam, crystal and shard damage all scale with your damage bonuses
		Each beam slices the same enemy up to 4 times per second for 35 base damage
		Enemies shattering a crystal take 70 base damage and are struck by shards dealing 40 each
		Hits inflict Refraction: the target slows and your crit chance against it rises by 8%
		"When the light-web takes shape, the one dancing to the music owns the ballroom"
		'''
}

TwinPupilTether: {
	DisplayName: Twin-Pupil Tether
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons Vision and Pyrepupil, a pair of orbiting mini mechanical eyes; their damage scales with your damage bonuses
		Vision snipes mid-range enemies with lasers: 140 base damage per shot, about one shot every 0.7 seconds
		Pyrepupil breathes cursed flames at nearby enemies: 40 base damage per gout, five gouts per second
		A cutting tether is always strung between the eyes, slicing the same enemy up to 4 times per second for 80 base damage
		Cut enemies are torn open for 3 seconds, taking 25% more damage from the pair
		The faster you move, the wider the eyes spread and the longer the tether stretches
		Double tap Down to order a cross charge: the eyes flank your cursor, dash through each other, and detonate at the crossing point
		The charge impact deals 380 and the crossing detonation 1100 base damage, with a 9 second cooldown
		"A stitched gaze, and the thread that cuts everything"
		'''
}

ProbeMatrixCore: {
	DisplayName: Probe Matrix Core
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Deploys five Destroyer probes as an escort formation that seeks enemies and fires homing lasers
		Lasers deal 55 base damage; hits on the same target build designation, and 8 stacks call an orbital strike
		The strike drops a piercing deathray from the sky, dealing 900 base damage per tick
		Targets caught in the column take at most two ticks per strike, up to 1800 base damage total
		Designation resets after each strike with a 3 second cooldown, and the impact site lingers with searing heat
		Probes shot down by enemies rebuild after about 2.5 seconds; the formation uses no minion slots
		"The iron serpent has fallen, yet its eyes still patrol the sky for you"
		'''
}

OverloadCommandCore: {
	DisplayName: Overload Command Core
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Striking enemies builds ion charge: +4 per hit, Ion Overload triggers at 100
		Stop attacking for over a second and the charge slowly drains
		Ion Overload lasts 5 seconds, increasing attack speed by 30%
		While overloaded, your hits arc chain lightning between nearby enemies, jumping up to 3 times
		Each arc deals 40% of the triggering hit's damage, decaying per jump
		Four phantom mechanical arms unfold behind you, striking in sync with your attacks
		With a melee weapon the arms sweep, each blow dealing 24% weapon damage
		With any other weapon the arms fire ion bolts, each dealing 20% weapon damage
		When the overload ends, the core overheats for 3 seconds: 8% reduced attack speed and no charge gain
		"Command authority transferred. Four arms at your service, until meltdown"
		'''
}

BloomNovaBulb: {
	DisplayName: Bloom Nova Bulb
	Tooltip:
		'''
		+30 max life and +4 life regeneration
		When struck, lashes thorn vines at your attacker or toward the incoming threat, at most once every 1.5 seconds
		Vines deal 220 to 330 base damage depending on Growth, scaling with your damage bonuses
		Snared enemies are slowed and torn for 80 damage per second; bosses are only slightly slowed
		Snared enemies that hit you suffer thorn backlash: the full damage dealt plus 120 base damage
		Thorn backlash triggers at most once per half second on each enemy
		Fighting builds Growth: more vines that snare longer
		Below 35% life, a Bloom Nova erupts: a petal shockwave of 1200 base damage sweeps and snares nearby enemies
		The bloom instantly restores 25% of your life, greatly boosts regeneration for 6 seconds, and consumes all Growth
		Spore fog follows you for 6 seconds afterward; enemies in the fog miss 25% of their attacks
		Bloom Nova occurs at most once every 60 seconds
		"Every wound waters the next bloom"
		'''
}

SolarCoreFist: {
	DisplayName: Solar Core Fist
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Stand still for half a second to enter Stone Guard stance
		While in stance, damage taken is reduced by 50% and you are immune to knockback
		Each hit taken in stance grants 1 stack of Solar Charge, plus 1 extra per 100 raw damage of the blow
		Charge caps at 24 stacks; the shell veins brighten one tier per 8 stacks
		Holding the stance for 5 seconds forces a 2 second overheat: no damage reduction, no charge, no re-entering stance
		Hold DOWN for half a second in stance to hurl a full-power fist toward your cursor with a larger solar nova
		Moving also breaks the stance and throws the fist, but at 25% reduced damage
		Throwing the fist ends the stance without overheating
		The fist deals 500 base damage, +12.5% per stack, 2000 at full charge, scaling with your damage bonuses
		The first enemy struck erupts in a solar nova, chaining six lava bursts to both sides
		At 8 or more stacks, the stance radiates a scorching aura that scales with your damage bonuses
		"The temple's sun gem still beats; the stone shell is merely its gauntlet"
		'''
}

TidalFin: {
	DisplayName: Tidal Fin
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Press [KEY] to dash toward the cursor; press again shortly after to chain, up to two dashes
		Every dash can be re-aimed, and you are fully invincible while dashing
		Each dash raises a lingering tsunami wall along its path, dealing 140 base damage per hit
		Multiple walls do not stack their hits on the same target
		The wall shoves away and slows small hostile projectiles
		The final dash raises a stationary tidal tornado at its endpoint, grinding for 200 base damage per hit
		Wall and tornado damage scales with your damage bonuses
		While it rains or you are submerged, the chain gains a third dash and all damage is boosted by 50%
		The full chain has a 12 second cooldown
		[c/2696A0:"The tide has not forgotten its duke"]
		'''
}

RiteRing: {
	DisplayName: Rite Ring
	Tooltip:
		'''
		8% increased damage, +40 maximum mana, and each lit rune grants 1% more damage
		Attacking or casting lights runes around you; at 8 runes the current rite fires automatically
		Rites rotate in order: Mirror Rite, Moonflame Laser, Star Rite
		Mirror Rite: conjures 3 pale mirror bodies, each firing 3 volleys of your held weapon's shots at 40% damage
		Summon, held-style and explosive weapons cannot be mirrored; mirrors fire rune bolts instead
		Moonflame Laser: a moon eye opens overhead and sweeps the field with a death ray
		Star Rite: a tiny planetary ring collapses, calling down 16 falling stars upon your foes
		Double tap Left or Right to spend 3 runes, tearing the veil for a short blink in that direction
		"The rite began long ago, and you are standing at the circle's heart"
		'''
}

WingsOfInterference: {
	DisplayName: Wings of Interference
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Become the wings of the Empress of Light: 3.5s of flight time by day and 4.5s by night, hold DOWN while flying to hover
		Day form: your attack projectiles trace interference light-paths as they fly
		When two light-paths cross, the intersection detonates a prism burst dealing 200 base damage
		Night form: noticeably increased movement speed and longer flight time
		At night, automatically dodge one hit, once every 48 seconds
		At night, hostile projectiles closing in on you drag auroral trails, exposing their paths early
		The instant dawn or dusk arrives, a screen-wide interference burst deals 1100 base damage and clears hostile projectiles
		"Day and night interfere at the wingtip; light collapses where paths cross"
		'''
	FormDay: It is day now: the interference weave is deployed
	FormNight: It is night now: swift auroral flight is engaged
}

BlackFlashSigil: {
	DisplayName: Black Flash Sigil
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Attacking awakens the sigil; a black flash tempo ring lights up on your chest
		The instant the ring contracts to its smallest, the judgment window opens with a sharp chime
		Hits landed within the window trigger a Black Flash: that strike deals 3x damage and always crits
		Each Black Flash adds 1 Flash Chain stack; every stack adds another 0.25x, capped at 6 stacks for 4.5x
		Higher chains quicken the tempo; the next window comes ever sooner
		Letting a window pass empty, or landing hits outside it, clears every stack
		At 4 stacks you enter Domain Sense; projectiles around you seem to slow
		Minions act on their own; they neither follow the tempo nor break the chain
		"When the flash turns black, the instant reigns over eternity"
		'''
}
